==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|perturben}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|perturber}}, from {{der|en|la|perturbo|perturbare|throw into confusion, confuse, disorder, disturb}}, from {{m|la|per||through}} + {{m|la|turbo|turbare|to confuse, disturb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/pɚˈtɝb/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-perturb.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(r)b}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[disturb]]; to bother or unsettle.
# {{lb|en|physics}} To slightly modify the motion of an object.
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} To modify the motion of a body by exerting a gravitational force.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} To modify slightly, such as an equation or value.

====Derived terms====
